    "lastText": "The `minisheet` engine is built as specified. All 82 tests pass with `npm test`, and the changes are uncommitted in the working tree.\n\n**What's there**\n- `src/sheet.js` exports `Sheet`, with `set`, `get`, and `getInput`, plus the literal rules and the reference handling from TASK.md.\n- The formula parser, with the operator precedence table (including `-2^2` = 4 and right-associative `^`), is in `src/parser.js`.\n- All 55 functions the spec lists are in `src/functions.js`. Helper modules are `src/values.js` and `src/refs.js`.\n- `README.md` lists every function and documents the behaviour choices below.\n- Tests are in `test/`: API, formulas, functions, and cycles. They run on `node --test` with no dependencies.\n\n**Judgment calls where the spec was silent**\n- `COUNTBLANK` counts `\"\"` as blank, as Excel does.\n- `ISBLANK`, `ISNUMBER`, `ISTEXT`, and `ISLOGICAL` propagate errors, because the spec's exception list only names `IFERROR`, `IFNA`, `ISERROR`, and `ISNA`.\n- Cycle detection is static: a self-reference inside an untaken `IF` branch still gives `#CIRC!`.\n- An empty cell compares as `FALSE` against booleans.\n- `SUM()` with no arguments is `#VALUE!` (wrong argument count), while `MIN`, `MAX`, and `PRODUCT` with no numbers give 0.\n- A numeric criterion only matches numeric cells.\n- `REPT` results over 32767 characters give `#VALUE!`.\n- A bare name that is not a function or a cell gives `#NAME?`.\n\n**Performance:** a graph rebuild only happens when a formula cell changes. A 1000-formula sheet with 1000 set-and-get rounds takes about 50ms.",
